EastSun 20260930 (on the events table): "你確定這是件是WPF 操作相似? 你去網路上搜尋 WPF
相關手冊或說明", then "我需要你把此外掛軟體改得跟WPF 操作模式一樣" and "一小部分一小部分
搜尋、小部分修改、一直持續下去". Part 1, from Microsoft's own steps
("How to: Create a Simple Event Handler" (WPF Designer), "How to add or remove an
event handler" (Windows Forms)):
- two columns, the event | its handler. Nothing under the rows any more (no
  code rows, chips, 「其他找到的地方」); where it is wired -- the C++ that runs and
  its line, the WS command, the server, BCB6's name and line -- is the row's
  tooltip. The name no longer wraps letter by letter.
- an empty one is empty (no grey default name that looked set).
- "Type the event handler name or leave it blank to use the default name. To
  create the event handler, press ENTER or double-click the value column."
- a set one: a double-click goes to its code (the function that runs).
- the value's list = "all methods that have a compatible method signature":
  the form class's public methods with the event's parameter types and a
  compiled body (sbtExitClick yes; the GATE spbSaveClick no). Picking one =
  the event uses it: only the wiring is added, no code; one handler may serve
  several events (the generated table keys a row by control + event and finds
  the control's row first, for its Sender).
- right-click: jump to the code / all the code found... / Reset. Reset (or the
  name cleared + Enter) takes the page's htdCpp line and the generated row off;
  the C++ function stays ("you can't just delete handler code"). BCB6's .dfm
  ones and another page script's are read only (blue), refused for Reset.
- the panel's search also reads an event row's tooltip (spbSaveClick finds
  OnClick, whose value is the function that runs).
- vscode_it.ps1: the "extension cannot write" rule looks for write CALLS
  (fs.writeFile(...)), not a method of that name -- the read-only golden file
  provider's writeFile(uri) { throw NoPermissions } made it never apply; main.html
  was changed by another session at 16:06 (the 1.5x menus) during the run.

Tests (lib 158, smoke 160, panels, real VS Code 147): panels (two columns only,
nothing under the rows, empty really empty, the .dfm one read only with its
BCB6 line in the tooltip; blank + Enter = the default; a typed name + Enter
sent once; the right-click menu), smoke (the list, Reset keeps the C++, an
existing method for a second event = wiring only, a .dfm one not reset).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
